  "worked_solution": "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nSince the object's initial position is $(2,0),$ we have that $r(0)=\\,2i,$ and we can conclude that the radius of the circle $R=2.$\n\nTherefore, since we have $R=2$ and $\\omega =-3\\text{\u00a0rad/s}$ (negative because the motion is clockwise), we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =2(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(-3t)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-3t)\\,j) \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{cos}\u20613t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}\u20613t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
